{"type":"message","id":"42c0bf97","parentId":"4efab9b1","timestamp":"2026-02-16T15:50:24.296Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Identifying Configuration Files**\n\nI am now focusing on identifying the relevant configuration files. My initial plan involves checking the current directory and its subdirectories. I need to pinpoint which files contain the user's settings to ensure only those files are pushed to GitHub. This is where I am focused at present.\n\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<think>The user wants to update their settings to GitHub.\nI am in `/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace`.\nI should:\n1. Check the git status in the workspace.\n2. If it's a repo, add the changes and commit/push.\n3. If not, I might need to initialize it or check where the \"settings\" are (maybe the OpenClaw config?).\n\nWait, the user said \"지금 셋팅\" (current settings). This could mean the OpenClaw configuration or the workspace files (AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, etc.). Given the context of \"OpenClaw assistant\", they likely mean the workspace files and possibly the gateway config.\n\nLet's check the git status first.\nI'll also read the `github` skill as instructed by the \"Skills (mandatory)\" section.</think>"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"read_1771257024226_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/github/SKILL.md"},"thoughtSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":""}],"api":"google-gemini-cli","provider":"google-antigravity","model":"gemini-3-flash","usage":{"input":14795,"output":409,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15204,"cost":{"input":0.0073974999999999996,"output":0.001227,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0086245}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771257020190}}
{"type":"message","id":"1eea09a4","parentId":"42c0bf97","timestamp":"2026-02-16T15:50:24.307Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read_1771257024226_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: github\ndescription: \"Interact with GitHub using the `gh` CLI. Use `gh issue`, `gh pr`, `gh run`, and `gh api` for issues, PRs, CI runs, and advanced queries.\"\nmetadata:\n  {\n    \"openclaw\":\n      {\n        \"emoji\": \"🐙\",\n        \"requires\": { \"bins\": [\"gh\"] },\n        \"install\":\n          [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"brew\",\n              \"kind\": \"brew\",\n              \"formula\": \"gh\",\n              \"bins\": [\"gh\"],\n              \"label\": \"Install GitHub CLI (brew)\",\n            },\n            {\n              \"id\": \"apt\",\n              \"kind\": \"apt\",\n              \"package\": \"gh\",\n              \"bins\": [\"gh\"],\n              \"label\": \"Install GitHub CLI (apt)\",\n            },\n          ],\n      },\n  }\n---\n\n# GitHub Skill\n\nUse the `gh` CLI to interact with GitHub. Always specify `--repo owner/repo` when not in a git directory, or use URLs directly.\n\n## Pull Requests\n\nCheck CI status on a PR:\n\n```bash\ngh pr checks 55 --repo owner/repo\n```\n\nList recent workflow runs:\n\n```bash\ngh run list --repo owner/repo --limit 10\n```\n\nView a run and see which steps failed:\n\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --repo owner/repo\n```\n\nView logs for failed steps only:\n\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --repo owner/repo --log-failed\n```\n\n## API for Advanced Queries\n\nThe `gh api` command is useful for accessing data not available through other subcommands.\n\nGet PR with specific fields:\n\n```bash\ngh api repos/owner/repo/pulls/55 --jq '.title, .state, .user.login'\n```\n\n## JSON Output\n\nMost commands support `--json` for structured output. You can use `--jq` to filter:\n\n```bash\ngh issue list --repo owner/repo --json number,title --jq '.[] | \"\\(.number): \\(.title)\"'\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771257024304}}
