{"type":"message","id":"406b45cf","parentId":"1ed4dee4","timestamp":"2026-02-17T22:04:37.999Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sam noticed that the same message appeared twice.\nChecking the cron history for `daily-morning-briefing`:\n- Yesterday's run: `ts: 1771279286837`\n- Today's run: `ts: 1771365697104`\n\nThe *content* of the briefings is different (Tuesday vs Wednesday), so it's not the same briefing repeating.\nHowever, if Sam is seeing the exact same *response* from me (the user-facing greeting) twice in the chat:\n1. It might be a Telegram delivery retry issue.\n2. It might be because the `[System Message]` was delivered as a system event *and* I manually responded to it.\n3. OpenClaw might have sent a \"streaming preview\" and then a \"final message\" separately.\n\nWait, I see what happened. In the previous turn, I provided the briefing. Then, a system prompt for \"Pre-compaction memory flush\" arrived.\nIf Sam is referring to the *briefing* itself:\nLooking at the chat history provided in the prompt:\n- I sent the briefing once at 07:05 KST.\n- There are no duplicate messages visible in the provided context for *this* session.\n\nWait, looking at the `openclaw status --deep` output from earlier, I saw:\n```\n│ agent:main:cron:eb4407c8-7e9a-4…                             │ direct │ 29m ago  │ gemini-3-flash │ 8.6k/200k (4%)  │\n│ agent:main:cron:eb4407c8-7e9a-4…                             │ direct │ 29m ago  │ gemini-3-flash │ 8.6k/200k (4%)  │\n```\nThere are **two concurrent sessions** for the same cron job ID. This usually happens if the gateway thinks a job is still running and triggers it again, or if there's a race condition in the scheduler.\n\nI will investigate the cron job configuration and the `eb4407c8-7e9a-4d66-b956-2695d5aee260` job specifically."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"cron_1771365877924_191","name":"cron","arguments":{"action":"list"},"thoughtSignature":"EiYKJGUyNDgzMGE3LTVjZDYtNDJmZS05OThiLWVlN