{"type":"message","id":"8aa513d6","parentId":"dfe979e1","timestamp":"2026-02-18T09:52:54.765Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Correcting Tool Schema**\n\nI've hit a snag with the `cron` tool. I was mistaken; `notify` isn't a top-level property within the `add` action's schema. It seems I may have conflated it with the `delivery` options, or perhaps it's a legacy element. I'm double-checking the definition now within the system prompt to eliminate any lingering ambiguity and ensure data integrity.\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"cron_1771408373951_5","name":"cron","arguments":{"action":"add","job":{"schedule":{"kind":"cron","tz":"Asia/Seoul","expr":"0 4 * * *"},"payload":{"message":"Execute the backup script at /home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/backup_to_github.sh using the exec tool. If it fails, report the error. If successful, simply confirm the backup is done.","kind":"agentTurn"},"enabled":true,"name":"daily-github-backup","delivery":{"mode":"none"},"sessionTarget":"isolated"}},"thoughtSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":""}],"api":"google-gemini-cli","provider":"google-antigravity","model":"gemini-3-pro-high","usage":{"input":4682,"output":383,"cacheRead":466999,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":472064,"cost":{"input":0.009363999999999999,"output":0.004596,"cacheRead":0.0933998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.1073598}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771408351417}}
