{"type":"message","id":"004c454a","parentId":"966f0f90","timestamp":"2026-02-18T10:05:11.845Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Updating Service Restart Policy**\n\nI'm updating the OpenClaw systemd service configuration based on Sam's specifications. The goal is to enhance stability while preventing update conflicts.\n\nThe new configuration will be:\n- `Restart=on-failure`: Restarts only on crashes, preventing loops during manual stops for updates.\n- `RestartSec=5`: Adds a 5-second delay before restarting.\n- `StartLimitBurst=10` & `StartLimitIntervalSec=60`: Allows up to 10 restarts within a minute.\n\nI'll modify the service file at `~/.config/systemd/user/openclaw-gateway.service`, reload the systemd daemon, and verify the service status.\n\n\n[Historical context: a different model called tool \"edit\" with arguments: {\n  \"newText\": \"Restart=on-failure\\nRestartSec=5\\nStartLimitIntervalSec=60\\nStartLimitBurst=10\\n\",\n  \"path\": \"/home/lfant/.config/systemd/user/openclaw-gateway.service\",\n  \"oldText\": \"Restart=always\\nRestartSec=5\\n\"\n}. Do not mimic this format - use proper function calling.]"}],"api":"google-gemini-cli","provider":"google-antigravity","model":"gemini-3-pro-high","usage":{"input":474312,"output":266,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":474578,"cost":{"input":0.9486239999999999,"output":0.003192,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.9518159999999999}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1771409103043}}
