{"type":"message","id":"3a69414f","parentId":"e462085a","timestamp":"2026-02-18T11:50:20.319Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Analyzing Installation Failure**\n\nThe installation failed again with the same \"No such device or address\" error at line 85, even in non-interactive mode. I've examined the script source, and it explicitly checks for `/dev/tty` or a terminal on stdin, failing if neither is present, *unless* `NON_INTERACTIVE=\"true\"`. However, the check at line 85 seems to happen *before* the argument parsing loop fully takes effect or the logic is flawed in the specific version I fetched.\n\nWait, looking at the script source I fetched:\n```bash\nsetup_tty() {\n  if [[ -t 0 ]]; then\n    # ...\n  elif [[ -e /dev/tty ]]; then\n    # ...\n  else\n    # No terminal available at all\n    if [[ \"$NON_INTERACTIVE\" != \"true\" ]]; then\n      echo \"Error: No terminal available...\" >&2\n      exit 1\n    fi\n  fi\n}\n```\nIf `NON_INTERACTIVE` is true, it shouldn't exit. But the error `main: line 85: /dev/tty: No such device or address` suggests it's trying to access `/dev/tty` regardless, or my `NON_INTERACTIVE` variable isn't being passed correctly to the piped bash process.\n\nWhen I run `curl ... | bash -s -- --non-interactive ...`, the arguments are passed to bash, but the script needs to parse them. The `setup_tty` function is called early.\n\nThe error `main: line 85` in the output corresponds to:\n```bash\n    exec 3</dev/tty\n```\nAh, looking at the code again:\n```bash\n  elif [[ -e /dev/tty ]]; then\n    # stdin is piped (curl | bash) but /dev/tty is available\n    exec 3</dev/tty\n    TTY_FD=3\n```\nIf `/dev/tty` exists (which it might in some restricted environments, or the check `-e` passes but `open` fails), it tries to `exec 3</dev/tty`. If the environment claims `/dev/tty` exists but it's not actually usable (e.g. in a non-interactive runner), it crashes.\n\n**Solution:**\nI will bypass the installer script entirely and perform the installation steps manually, as I can see exactly what the script does:\n1.  Installs `bun` (if missing).\n2.  Installs `uv` (if missing).\n3.  Clones the `claude-mem` repo.\n4.  Builds the plugin using `npm install` and `tsc`.\n5.  Creates a minimal `package.json` for the plugin.\n6.  Installs the plugin into OpenClaw via `openclaw plugins install`.\n7.  Enables it via `openclaw plugins enable`.\n8.  Configures `settings.json`.\n\nI will start by checking for `bun` and `uv`, then proceed with the clone and build.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_1771415420233_41","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"npm install -g bun"},"thoughtSignature":"EiYKJGUyNDgzMGE3LTVjZDYtNDJmZS05OThiLWVlNTM5ZTcyYjljMw=="},{"type":"text","text":""}],"api":"google-gemini-cli","provider":"google-antigravity","model":"gemini-3-pro-high","usage":{"input":21215,"output":686,"cacheRead":534677,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":556578,"cost":{"input":0.042429999999999995,"output":0.008232,"cacheRead":0.10693540000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.1575974}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771415350420}}
