{"type":"message","id":"032f5f79","parentId":"bd2eb662","timestamp":"2026-02-18T23:20:53.061Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Investigating Log Anomalies**\n\nI've noticed something off: only `config-audit.jsonl` is showing up in the logs. Gateway and session logs are typically present. The gateway logs might be managed by systemd, since it's running as a service. I should be able to check them using `journalctl`.\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_1771456852300_48","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"journalctl --user -u openclaw-gateway -n 100 --no-pager"},"thoughtSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":""}],"api":"google-gemini-cli","provider":"google-antigravity","model":"gemini-3-pro-high","usage":{"input":587711,"output":158,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":587869,"cost":{"input":1.175422,"output":0.0018960000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":1.1773179999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771456838749}}
