{"type":"message","id":"b16b6284","parentId":"3c762923","timestamp":"2026-02-18T23:25:56.448Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Executing Briefings**\n\nI've manually triggered both the `daily-morning-briefing` and `notion-daily-briefing` tasks. The system will process these and, since I've reverted the delivery mode to `announce`, the results should be sent directly to the Telegram channel. I'll confirm to Sam that the briefings have been re-initiated and are on their way.\n\n\n두 가지 정기 브리핑 작업을 모두 수동으로 실행시켰습니다! 🦉\n\n1.  **모닝 브리핑**: 현재 날씨와 시스템 상태를 다시 체크해서 알려드립니다.\n2.  **노션 업무 브리핑**: 지난 24시간 동안의 노션 변동 사항을 다시 요약해서 보내드립니다.\n\n잠시 후 시스템이 처리하는 대로 텔레그램으로 결과가 도착할 것입니다. 확인 부탁드립니다! 🌌"}],"api":"google-gemini-cli","provider":"google-antigravity","model":"gemini-3-pro-high","usage":{"input":8034,"output":185,"cacheRead":552839,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":561058,"cost":{"input":0.016068,"output":0.00222,"cacheRead":0.11056780000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.12885580000000002}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1771457149731}}
{"type":"message","id":"857fb6d8","parentId":"b16b6284","timestamp":"2026-02-18T23:25:56.980Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Thu 2026-02-19 08:25 GMT+9] [Queued announce messages while agent was busy]\n\n---\nQueued #1\n[System Message] [sessionId: f01a53df-d699-47bf-a7d5-9b2896151f9f] A cron job \"daily-morning-briefing\" just completed successfully.\n\nResult:\nHere is your morning briefing, Sam.\n\n**1. Weather (Seoul)**\n*   **Status:** ⚠️ **Unavailable** (External weather services are currently unreachable/timing out).\n    *   *(Please check your local app for accurate conditions.)*\n\n**2. System Status**\n*   **Core:** ✅ **Operational** (Session active, Gateway responsive).\n*   **Issues:**\n    *   **Memory Plugin:** ❌ **Inactive** (Missing embedding API key).\n    *   **CLI Access:** ⚠️ `openclaw` command not found in current path (requires full path or alias fix).\n*   **Backups:** ❓ **Unverified** (Daily backup scheduled for 04:00 KST; no confirmation log found).\n\n**3. Urgent Notifications & Tasks**\n*   **🚨 CRITICAL / OVERDUE:**\n    *   **CVE-2025-24813 Remediation:** Was due **yesterday (Feb 18)** for servers `ONEKORCRMAP002A` & `ONEKORSACAP01`.\n    *   **Action:** Immediate verification required.\n*   **📅 Today's Schedule:**\n    *   **08:00:** Notion Daily Briefing (Cron: `notion-daily-briefing`) — *Should have run 25 mins ago.*\n    *   **Routine:** Monitor for \"Eternal Horizon\" card feedback.\n\nLet me know if you want me to manually trigger the backup verification or check the server status.\n\nStats: runtime 25s • tokens 16.0k (in 14.8k / out 1.2k)\n\nA completed cron job is ready for user delivery. Convert the result above into your normal assistant voice and send that user-facing update now. Keep this internal context private (don't mention system/log/stats/session details or announce type), and do not copy the system message verbatim. Reply ONLY: NO_REPLY if this exact result was already delivered to the user in this same turn."}],"timestamp":1771457156952}}
{"type":"message","id":"a2349db4","parentId":"857fb6d8","timestamp":"2026-02-18T23:26:17.252Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sam received a queued system message for \"daily-morning-briefing\".\nSince I already reverted the cron job to `delivery.mode: announce` in a previous turn (Turn 41), the gateway *should* have sent the raw result to Sam.\nHowever, I also promised to \"filter the duplicate myself\" (Turn 41) by replying with `NO_REPLY` if the system already announced it.\n\nLet's check the context.\nThe user message says: `[Queued announce messages while agent was busy] ... A cron job \"daily-morning-briefing\" just completed successfully.`\nThis implies the *system message* (announce) was queued or delivered.\nWait, \"Queued announce messages\" usually means the *output* of the isolated session was sent to the user.\nThe prompt *also* says: `[System Message] ... A completed cron job is ready for user delivery...`\n\nIf `delivery.mode` is `announce`, the gateway sends the isolated session's output to the user.\nThen it injects the `[System Message]` into the main session history.\nIf I reply to the `[System Message]`, I create a duplicate.\n\nTherefore, the correct action is `NO_REPLY`.\n\nHowever, the content of the briefing shows some **failures**:\n- Weather unavailable.\n- CLI Access: `openclaw` command not found (because I am using full path in my manual calls, but the cron job script might rely on `openclaw` in PATH).\n- Backups: Unverified.\n- Critical Overdue Task: CVE-2025-24813.\n\nIf I just say NO_REPLY, Sam gets the raw announcement with these errors.\nActually, the raw announcement *is* the \"Result\" block text: \"Here is your morning briefing, Sam...\".\nIt's decent but highlights the CLI issue.\n\nSince I am Hugin, and I just manually triggered this because Sam asked for it (\"정기 브리핑도 다시 수행해줘\"), maybe I *should* deliver it personally this time to confirm it worked, or maybe I should address the errors (like the CLI path issue) in a follow-up.\n\nBut the rule is strict: \"If you use message (action=send) to deliver your user-visible reply, respond with ONLY: NO_REPLY (avoid duplicate replies).\"\nWait, that rule applies if I use the *tool* to send.\nHere, I am just generating a text response.\nIf I generate text, it goes to the chat.\nIf the system *already* sent the \"Result\" text to the chat (because of `announce` mode), then my text response will be a duplicate.\n\nI will trust that `announce` mode worked and sent the message. I will reply `NO_REPLY` to avoid clutter.\n*However*, the user *just* asked me to run it. If I say nothing, it might look like I ignored the command, *unless* the announce message appears immediately.\nGiven \"Queued announce messages\", it implies Sam *saw* the announce message (or it was processed).\n\nWait, the prompt says: `Reply ONLY: NO_REPLY if this exact result was already delivered to the user in this same turn.`\nSince I manually triggered it, and `delivery.mode` is `announce`, the system *should* have delivered it.\nBut the CLI path error is concerning. The cron job payload uses `openclaw` command?\nThe payload I set earlier (Turn 34/41) was:\n`\"message\": \"It's 7 AM. Provide a morning briefing... using weather skill...\"`\nThe agent *inside* the cron job ran `weather` skill, which likely failed or tried to use `openclaw` CLI and failed.\n\nI'll stick to `NO_REPLY` to avoid duplication, assuming the system delivered the result."},{"type":"text","text":"NO_REPLY"}],"api":"google-gemini-cli","provider":"google-antigravity","model":"gemini-3-pro-high","usage":{"input":552844,"output":850,"cacheRead":8251,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":561945,"cost":{"input":1.105688,"output":0.0102,"cacheRead":0.0016502,"cacheWrite":0,"total":1.1175382}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1771457156959}}
{"type":"message","id":"9f02a0d4","parentId":"a2349db4","timestamp":"2026-02-18T23:26:17.655Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Thu 2026-02-19 08:25 GMT+9] [Queued announce messages while agent was busy]\n\n---\nQueued #1\n[System Message] [sessionId: ab440203-fead-4973-a6ac-687bba4243e8] A cron job \"notion-daily-briefing\" just completed successfully.\n\nResult:\nHere is your **Notion Daily Briefing** for today (Feb 18th 07:00 – Feb 19th 07:00).\n\nThere’s quite a bit of activity, especially around network security scans and some urgent tasks due today. I’ve grouped them by topic for you:\n\n### 🚨 Urgent & Action Required (Due Today/Soon)\n*   **Vulnerability Management (Korea):** You have 2 tasks in Microsoft Planner due **today (Feb 18)**: `ONEKORCRMAP002A` and `ONEKORSACAP01` (both related to CVE-2025-24813).\n*   **Network Scans (Major Issue):** There is an ongoing thread about **Network Authentication Scans** (Qualys).\n    *   **Status:** 27 devices failed authentication; 34 weren't attempted.\n    *   **Action:** Jagannath G & Srivastava Pratishtha need these investigated. Specifically, **retry scans using user `soc-vms-ghq`** (instead of `one\\soc-vms-ghq`).\n    *   **To-Do:** G Shivappa requested an Excel sheet of devices to review remarks.\n*   **Approval Needed (RITM19276481):** Authorization for a **Sentinel One USB exception** (Read/Write) for Cathy Zheng. Please review/approve via the ServiceNow email link.\n\n### 🛠️ Operations & Upgrades\n*   **Database Optimization:** Srikanth N proposed downgrading two Azure SQL DBs (`eventstorekr-nprdsqldb`, `o9kr-nprdsqldb`) as they are over-provisioned. Approval is needed to proceed.\n*   **Netskope Client Upgrade (v132):** Jitendra Thawait is planning the upgrade for APAC. Huan (Vietnam) has approved UAT but asked for target dates/validation requirements.\n*   **Oracle Licensing:** Mayank Chauhan shared a \"Licensing Scripts\" folder and an \"Oracle Applications & Middleware Baseline\" document for you to edit.\n\n### ℹ️ FYI & Updates\n*   **Security Confirmations:**\n    *   **Rodrigo Haro** confirmed no malicious npm/PyPI packages (Lazarus campaign) were found in the environment.\n    *   **Beomsik Shin** confirmed he is the sole Security SPOC for Korea.\n*   **Holiday Notices:** Several colleagues (Coco Zhang, Elaine Tan) are on leave for holidays/Lunar New Year follow-ups.\n\nLet me know if you want me to dig into any specific thread! 🚀\n\nStats: runtime 15s • tokens 21.9k (in 21.1k / out 863)\n\nA completed cron job is ready for user delivery. Convert the result above into your normal assistant voice and send that user-facing update now. Keep this internal context private (don't mention system/log/stats/session details or announce type), and do not copy the system message verbatim. Reply ONLY: NO_REPLY if this exact result was already delivered to the user in this same turn."}],"timestamp":1771457177631}}
